1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,905
In 1692, Richard Coman told a Salem court about a night no one else could see.

2
00:00:05,905 --> 00:00:07,614
He said the house was locked.

3
00:00:07,614 --> 00:00:09,132
A light was burning.

4
00:00:09,132 --> 00:00:11,122
His wife lay beside him.

5
00:00:11,122 --> 00:00:13,456
Then Bridget Bishop entered the room.

6
00:00:13,456 --> 00:00:22,678
Coman said she lay across his chest and pressed him down so completely that he could neither speak nor move—not even enough to wake his wife.

7
00:00:22,678 --> 00:00:27,091
Years after the night itself, he put that memory under oath.

8
00:00:27,091 --> 00:00:30,918
Eight days after his testimony, Bridget Bishop was hanged.

9
00:00:30,918 --> 00:00:34,336
The record cannot tell us what state produced Coman's night.

10
00:00:34,336 --> 00:00:36,326
It tells us what Salem did with it.

